[node name="Version Text" type="Label" parent="Version Scrollbar" unique_id=674897346]
custom_minimum_size = Vector2(248, 0)
custom_maximum_size = Vector2(248, -1)
layout_mode = 2
offset_transform_enabled = true
offset_transform_position = Vector2(8, 0)
theme_override_colors/font_color = Color(0, 0, 0, 1)
text = "Version 1.6: The Big One
Sprint 6
Additions:
Levels 2 & 3 have been added!
Answer quizzes, flee a procedurally-generated tower, and collect a surprising quantity of baked goods!
Additionally, the new levels feature new art and music!
Changes:
Many placeholder sprites have been replaced with final versions
Level 1 has had significant overhauls in some areas
The menu screen now features proper visuals
Fixes:
Lots of small things, like a full softlock upon meeting the Hatter if your framerate isn't high enough
Other:
Hold Escape for 3 seconds to return to the menu
Press + to skip to the next level
Probably more belongs in each category but because of the crunch, time lost all meaning - see what you can find!

Version 1.5:
Sprint 5
Additions:
Level 1 has been implemented!
Try out levers and time-restricted abilities as you help the Cheshire Cat find his head!
Changes:
The finer details of movement have been adjusted (hangtime and input buffering, plus slight jump height increase) and should now better match player's intended inputs
A brand new textbox to go with a less obstructive ability UI
A character in the tutorial level has moved somewhere new...
Fixes:
The exit to the tutorial now functions, instead of trapping the player in an offscreen pit (The level 1 exit still will, however)

Version 1.4:
Sprint 4
Features:
The tutorial level is now complete!* It has a small area to test out each ability, and a secret to see other existing features...
Behind the scenes, all major level mechanics have basic functionality
Fixes:
The music now plays properly in the tutorial (a single bool was inverted, I was testing with sound off)
NPCs should no longer cut off their text early when spoken to multiple times
The credits finally autoscroll

Version 1.3:
Sprint 3
Features:
Added a tutorial level to show the new art and music (Layout still unfinished)
(The test plane contains more mechanics and can still be accessed from the bottom button)
Added an ability UI display to show which ones you have
Abilities can now have time or usage limits
Powerups can respawn after collection
Added a dialogue choice system
Partially implemented levers and doors
Fixes:
The player no longer rapidly slows at the end of a dash if still holding a movement key
Powerups types are now visibly different (still placeholders)
The jumping animation now plays properly
Guide to new things:
E on levers to open the doors, speak with the right NPC to initiate a dialogue choice, powerups with timers and respawns are found to the right in the test plane


Version 1.2:
Sprint 2
Features:
The map is now the test map, containing such additions as-
Powerups (enables double jump, wall jump, and dash(shift))
NPCs (e to interact)
Other additions:
Title screen music
A real sprite for the player
Coyote time to make platforming less frustrating
Fixes:
None

Version 1.1:
Sprint 1
Features:
Added a title screen
Added buttons
Added credits/version notes
Added WPI Splash
Added dash (shift)
Added walljump and double jump
Fixes:
None

Version 1.0:
Godot Tutorial Game
Features:
Followed Brackey's platformer tutorial
Added platforms that auto-detect walls
Fixes:
Stopped slimes from flying off cliffs
"
autowrap_mode = 2

